<div class="text-center">
	<h1 class="display-4">About Me</h1>
</div>

<div class="aboutMe">
	<p class="intro">Hi! I'm Megan of Meg's Cozy Crochet</p>
	<p>I've always had a creative side. In fact, I even won the art award back in public school! As I've gotten older, I've always needed something to keep both my hands and my imagination busy, and in 2024 I discovered crochet. What started as a way to channel my creativity quickly became a passion, and I fell in love with it almost immediately.</p>
	<img src="~/img/profile.JPG" alt="Megan Summers" />
	<p class="alt">One question my mom always asks is, "Are you using a pattern or just making it up?" More often than not, it's the latter. I love taking a photo, an idea, or even a simple description and figuring out how to bring it to life with yarn. Every project is a new challenge, and that's one of my favorite parts of crocheting.</p>
	<p>Whether it's a gift, a keepsake, a favorite character, or a piece of nostalgia, I believe the best creations are the ones that tell a story. Every piece is handmade with care, attention to detail, and just enough stubborn determination to convince yarn to become something extraordinary!</p>
	<p>The reason I started selling my creations is simple: I love seeing people get excited about them. There's something special about handing someone a finished piece and seeing the smile it brings to their face. Being able to share that joy with others is what inspired me to turn my passion into Meg's Cozy Crochet Crafts.</p>
	<img src="~/img/profilePic.JPG" alt="Megan Summers" />
	<p class="alt">Life is made of moments. I just happen to stitch them together!</p>
</div>